---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import DataHeader from "../../components/data/DataHeader.astro";
import BudgetExplorer from "../../components/data/BudgetExplorer.jsx";
import ServiceTrendExplorer from "../../components/data/ServiceTrendExplorer.jsx";
import PublicWorksBreakdown from "../../components/data/PublicWorksBreakdown.jsx";
import overview from "../../data/budget-overview.json";
import departments from "../../data/budget-departments-reported.json";
import reconciliation from "../../data/budget-reconciliation.json";
import serviceData from "../../data/service-net-requirements.json";
import serviceTaxLevy2026 from "../../data/service-tax-levy-2026.json";
import publicWorksComponents from "../../data/public-works-components.json";
import publicWorksAnnotations from "../../data/public-works-annotations.json";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Peterborough Budget Explorer | AJ Shearer"
  description="Explore Peterborough municipal budget figures from 2022 to 2026 with approved/final totals, normalized service trends, source links and explicit reconciliation status."
  canonical="https://vote.ajshearer.com/data/budget"
>
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-[#f8f1f3] text-[#3a1a22]">
    <DataHeader />
    <section class="border-b border-[#eadde1] bg-white">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
        <a href="/data" class="text-sm font-bold text-[#651024]">← Peterborough By The Numbers</a>
        <div class="mt-6 max-w-4xl">
          <div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-[#651024]">Budget explorer</div>
          <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-6xl">Where does the money go?</h1>
          <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">The operating-budget backbone covers 2022–2026, and the normalized service layer now includes stable five-year series plus qualified post-reorganization series where a clean 2022 bridge is not defensible. Approved prior-year numbers are taken from later City budget books wherever possible so draft and recommended figures do not quietly become final figures.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
      <aside class="mb-8 flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-[#d9c3ca] bg-[#fffafb] p-5 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
        <div><div class="font-black">Prefer the short version?</div><div class="mt-1 text-sm text-[#7a6167]">Start with the biggest comparable spending changes, then come back here for the full explorer.</div></div>
        <a href="/data/spending" class="shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[#651024] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-white">Read the 2-minute spending summary →</a>
      </aside>
      <section class="rounded-3xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-[#eadde1] md:p-9">
        <BudgetExplorer client:load overview={overview} departments={departments} reconciliation={reconciliation} />
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 rounded-3xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-[#eadde1] md:p-9">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#651024]">Normalized service trends</div>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Where is the growth actually showing up?</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-[#7a6167]">These series follow stable municipal services rather than department names. The trend measure is the City’s <strong>Net Requirement Before Indirect Revenues</strong>, recovered from approved prior-year columns and the final 2026 budget. For major 2026 services, the explorer also shows the bridge from that measure to <strong>Net Tax Levy</strong>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <ServiceTrendExplorer client:load serviceData={serviceData} levyBridge={serviceTaxLevy2026} />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 rounded-3xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-[#eadde1] md:p-9">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#651024]">Public Works deep dive</div>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">A reported jump that needs decomposition, not a headline.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-[#7a6167]">The Public Works total rises sharply in the 2025 approved presentation, but the component structure changes at the same time. This view separates the clean year-over-year comparisons from the structural break and identifies the snow-plowing change that can be sourced directly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <PublicWorksBreakdown client:load components={publicWorksComponents} annotations={publicWorksAnnotations} />
        </div>
        <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.peterborough.ca/media/21lhmi5p/budget-book-2026-final.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="rounded-full bg-[#651024] px-4 py-2 font-bold text-white">2026 final budget source ↗</a>
          <a href="https://pub-peterborough.escribemeetings.com/filestream.ashx?DocumentId=37183" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="rounded-full border border-[#c9aab3] bg-white px-4 py-2 font-bold text-[#651024]">Snow-plowing service report ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-5 ring-1 ring-[#eadde1]"><div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#651024]">Loaded</div><div class="mt-2 text-xl font-black">2022–2026 backbone</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-[#7a6167]">Gross operating totals, taxation revenue and source-reported department structures are in the warehouse.</p></div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-5 ring-1 ring-[#eadde1]"><div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#651024]">Live now</div><div class="mt-2 text-xl font-black">22 normalized service series</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-[#7a6167]">Stable five-year services plus qualified component series for Public Works, Recreation/Parks/Culture, IPGM and corporate administration where shorter windows are more defensible.</p></div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-5 ring-1 ring-[#eadde1]"><div class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#651024]">Crosswalk queue</div><div class="mt-2 text-xl font-black">Remaining crosswalk work</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-[#7a6167]">The major reorganization families are now exposed component-by-component with explicit start years. Full-term aggregate department claims remain intentionally withheld where scopes changed.</p></div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
